# Graphical code graphs

Follow [instructions/GRAPHICAL_CODE_GRAPHS.md](instructions/GRAPHICAL_CODE_GRAPHS.md) when drawing or updating a code-path graph (standalone HTML under `strategy/graphs/`, or a Cursor canvas).

- Stories on the left (one row each, blank cells when a stage does not run). Generous gaps so rails are traceable.
- Shared funnels and the real transformer are **one chip each**, with merge rails in and a consumer fan-out after.
- JS event chips sit where they fire (`glyphChanged`, `editingFontCompiled`, `glyphCanvasRendered`). Overview filter `EVENT_TYPES` sit after the change bridge.
- ChangeBridge is drawn once: local commits fan out into it; linked/remote windows fan in from it.
- DEL / CMB / RM badges mark unification. Start (green, left) and stop (red octagon, right) are visible only when the highlighted path uniquely begins or ends there.
- Hover lights in/out edges, full lanes, and a tiny legend above the details card. Ship the interactive HTML from `strategy/graphs/`; keep the Cursor canvas in sync when one exists.
- Manhattan paths. No per-row copies of a single sink. Keep node ids stable so git diffs stay readable.
